hey this is presh talwalkar  two candles of equal heights but  different thicknesses are lit  the first burns off in eight hours and  the second in ten hours  how long after lighting in hours will  the first candle be half the height of  the second candle  the candles are lit simultaneously and  each burns at a constant linear rate  i thank ryan from india for the  suggestion  pause the video if you'd like to give  this problem a try  and when you're ready keep watching to  learn how to solve this problem  [Music]  we can visualize the solution with the  help of a graph  let the vertical axis be the height of  the candle at a particular time and let  the x axis be the time that has elapsed  the first candle burns off in 8 hours  and the second candle burns off in 10  hours  each starts at the same height so we can  draw line segments from that same  starting point to the x-axis  the slope of the first line is negative  h over eight and the slope of the second  line is negative h over ten  so we can write equations for each of  these lines  the first line will be y one is equal to  negative h over eight multiplied by x  plus h and the second will be y two is  equal to negative h over ten multiplied  by x plus h  we want the time at which this line  segment is exactly equal to this line  segment that is the first candle is half  the height of the second candle  let's solve this algebraically  the second candle is exactly twice the  height of the first candle so y2 is  equal to 2 y1  we can substitute in and then we will  simplify each side of the equation  from here we can factor out an h term  from each side  let's continue to simplify this equation  since each side has a factor of h  the h will cancel out so it doesn't  depend on the initial height of the  candles  we then have negative x over ten plus  one is equal to negative x over four  plus two  we can then group like terms  one over 4 minus 1 over 10 is equal to 3  over 20.  we multiply both sides by 20 over 3 and  we get the answer that x is equal to 20  over 3 hours which is equal to 6 hours  and 40 minutes and that's the answer  thanks for making us one of the best  communities on youtube  see you next episode of mind your  decisions where we solve the world's  problems one video at a time
 

